Summary of Responsive Fixes
Global Overflow Lock: Added overflow-x: hidden and max-width: 100% to html, body. This is a fail-safe that strictly prevents horizontal scrolling, even if an unbreakable string (like a massive file path) manages to slip past the CSS wrappers.
Stacked Grid Layout: The @media (max-width: 768px) block changes .grid from 1fr 1fr to 1fr, instantly stacking the four parameter cards vertically for mobile viewing.
Touch-Target Buttons: The .actions and .confirm-ui containers switch to flex-direction: column on mobile. The buttons inside them are set to width: 100%, creating large, edge-to-edge tap targets that are much easier to hit with a thumb on a 390px display.
Word-Break on Receipts: Added word-break: break-word to #receipt-preview. This ensures that long, unbroken text strings (like local directory paths: C:\Users\Name\Pictures\...) will wrap to the next line instead of pushing the receipt container off-screen.
Dynamic Toast Sizing: The .toast notification is now anchored with left: 20px; right: 20px; instead of being fixed to the right side. This guarantees the notification bar spans cleanly across the bottom of narrow screens without clipping.
